      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZIPPING BELUGA (1) has been below best and missed the frame last couple, finishing 7th (31.82) last time in a Grade 6 at Angle Park. Is unbeaten in two runs at this course and distance. Strong form has emerged from his last run. Better than the latest effort and deserves another chance. DIVERGENCE (2) boxed on well to finish third last time, beaten 1.5 lengths (17.49) behind Connector at this track. Deserves a win and gets her chance. MISS PIPER (6) produced a moderate performance last time when sixth at Angle Park over 342m behind Kilcoy Lass (20.77) in a TG1-4W. Placed at her previous run. Got the money at her only try from this box. Cannot be taken lightly. BURNT TANGERINE (4) looks a chance coming off a five weeks layoff.",
